---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbJsonLd } from '../lib/seo';

const updated = 'August 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What data ReaderTweaks collects, why, and your choices. Short version: as little as possible."
  path="/privacy/"
  jsonLd={breadcrumbJsonLd([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy/' },
  ])}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap narrow prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The short version: ReaderTweaks collects as little as it can. There are no
        accounts, we do not sell or share your data for marketing, and any
        advertising the site carries is handled without profiling you across the
        web.
      </p>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>Only two things, and only when you choose to take part.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Newsletter email address.</strong> If you sign up for the
          newsletter, your email address is stored by our email provider,
          <a href="https://kit.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Kit</a> (formerly
          ConvertKit), so we can send you the newsletter. We ask you to confirm
          the address by email before anything is sent. You can unsubscribe from
          the link in any issue, which removes you from the list.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Anonymous traffic statistics.</strong> We use
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">
            Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>, which counts page views and referrers
          without cookies and without building a profile of you. It does not
          identify individual visitors.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not use Google Analytics or social-media tracking pixels.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising and sponsorships</h2>
      <p>
        ReaderTweaks is a commercial publication and may carry advertising and
        clearly labelled sponsorships, including in the newsletter. It does not
        currently run display advertising. If it does in future, any ad or
        sponsor slot will be labelled, and we will not add third-party ad
        networks that track you from site to site without updating this page to
        say what they collect and giving you a choice where the law requires one.
        How advertising relates to what we recommend is covered in the
        <a href="/about/#funding">editorial policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
      <p>
        Some links to accessories go to Amazon and include our Amazon Associates
        tag. If you buy something after clicking one, Amazon pays us a small
        commission at no extra cost to you. Amazon may set its own cookie when
        you follow the link; that is governed by
        <a href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/help/customer/display.html?nodeId=468496" rel="noopener" target="_blank">
          Amazon's privacy notice</a>, not ours. We never see who clicked or what
        they bought — only an aggregate commission total. As set out in the
        <a href="/about/#funding">editorial policy</a>, affiliate income does not
        decide which products we recommend.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        ReaderTweaks itself sets no cookies. Cloudflare may set a strictly
        functional cookie to keep the site secure and fast. If you interact with
        an embedded service — following an Amazon link, or submitting the
        newsletter form — that service may set its own cookies under its own
        policy.
      </p>

      <h2>Where the site is hosted</h2>
      <p>
        The site is served by Cloudflare Pages. Your request reaches Cloudflare's
        network, which processes connection data such as your IP address to
        deliver the page and block abuse. Cloudflare acts as our data processor
        for this.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Unsubscribe from the newsletter at any time using the link in any email.</li>
        <li>
          Ask us to delete your email address from our list, or to tell you what
          we hold, by writing to the address below.
        </li>
        <li>
          Depending on where you live (for example the EU, UK, or California) you
          may have additional rights to access, correct, or delete your data. We
          will honour those requests.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        ReaderTweaks is a technical reference for adults and is not directed at
        children under 13. We do not knowingly collect information from them.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the date at the top will change with it. Material
        changes will be noted in the newsletter.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions or requests:
        <a href="mailto:hello@readertweaks.com">hello@readertweaks.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .narrow { max-width: 720px; }
  .prose h1 { font-size: var(--step-3); }
  .prose h2 { margin-top: 2rem; }
  .updated { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--ink-faint); margin-top: 0.5rem; }
</style>
